SOURCE TO HTML:-

This project converts a C source file into an HTML file with syntax highlighting. The main.c file handles file operations, parser.c reads the 
source code character by character and identifies tokens like keywords, strings, numbers, comments, and preprocessor directives. Based on the 
token type, it calls functions in html.c, which generate HTML tags with different colors. The list of C keywords is maintained in keywords.c,
while style.h stores the HTML template and color definitions. Finally, the generated HTML file can be opened in a browser to view the source code 
in a colorized, readable format

Features

Converts C source code to HTML.
Syntax highlighting.
Supports line numbers (-n option).
Detects C keywords.
Highlights comments.
Highlights strings.
Highlights numbers.
Highlights character constants.
Highlights preprocessor directives.
Highlights header files.
Uses a black background similar to a code editor.